# Make sure elimination does not apply to an anti-join, which
# in MySQL's implementation is very similar to a LEFT JOIN and should
# not be confused with it. Elimination shouldn't apply to the
# semi-join either. For the anti-join transformation of NOT IN, the
# left and right arguments must not be nullable so we use COALESCE.
# For reference, we start with a LEFT JOIN which does elimination.
EXPLAIN SELECT DISTINCT t1.a FROM t1 LEFT JOIN t2 ON COALESCE(t1.a,0)=COALESCE(t2.b,0);
